  "clinical_evidence": [
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Good morning, doctor. Thank you for seeing me at such short notice. I'm afraid my joints have been giving me rather a lot of trouble, and I wasn't sure who else to ask.",
      "start_timestamp": "00:00",
      "end_timestamp": "00:17",
      "supports": [
        "chief_complaint"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Mainly my knees and the small joints of my hands. They ache, a deep sort of ache, and sometimes they feel as though they're slipping out of place.",
      "start_timestamp": "00:25",
      "end_timestamp": "00:39",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Ha. I bet it was. Do you remember when the aching actually began, as opposed to the party trick?",
      "start_timestamp": "01:13",
      "end_timestamp": "01:23",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]",
        "clinical_uncertainties[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "That's the difficult part, I'm afraid. I honestly can't say. It crept up. It might have been the summer, or it might have been before Christmas. I really couldn't tell you which.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:24",
      "end_timestamp": "01:42",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]",
        "clinical_uncertainties[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "I teach ballet, mostly to children, but I demonstrate every position myself, so I am on my feet and on my toes for most of the day.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:58",
      "end_timestamp": "02:14",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.social_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Dancing makes it worse by the evening, and a hot bath on Sunday helps a little. Though I wouldn't call it a cure.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:32",
      "end_timestamp": "02:43",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Any swelling in the joints, or redness? Anything you'd notice when you look at them?",
      "start_timestamp": "02:45",
      "end_timestamp": "02:54",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "No, no swelling that I've seen. They look quite ordinary, which is partly why I felt silly coming in.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:55",
      "end_timestamp": "03:07",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "You're not silly at all. Have you had any fever or feeling feverish, along with this?",
      "start_timestamp": "03:08",
      "end_timestamp": "03:16",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "No, no fever. I'd say I've felt perfectly well in myself, apart from being tired after a long teaching day.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:18",
      "end_timestamp": "03:29",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Only eczema, since I was a girl. It comes and goes, mostly on my elbows.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:37",
      "end_timestamp": "03:46",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Very sensible. Let me take your blood pressure first. It's 112 over 70, and your pulse is 66 and regular.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:12",
      "end_timestamp": "04:22",
      "supports": [
        "vital_signs[0]",
        "vital_signs[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Right. Your fingers bend back much further than normal, your thumb reaches your forearm, and both knees extend past straight. That's a sign of significantly lax joints.",
      "start_timestamp": "05:04",
      "end_timestamp": "05:17",
      "supports": [
        "physical_examination[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "It helps in ballet, but the same loose ligaments mean the muscles have to work much harder to hold the joint steady, and that tires and aches. So the most likely explanation is joint hypermobility.",
      "start_timestamp": "05:30",
      "end_timestamp": "05:50",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_assessment[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Fair question. I can't rule out an inflammatory arthritis yet, which is why I'd like to do some checks rather than assume.",
      "start_timestamp": "06:01",
      "end_timestamp": "06:14",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_assessment[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "I'll order blood tests for inflammation, and an X-ray of both knees, to look at the joints themselves.",
      "start_timestamp": "06:23",
      "end_timestamp": "06:33",
      "supports": [
        "procedures_and_investigations[0]",
        "procedures_and_investigations[1]",
        "clinical_actions[0]",
        "clinical_actions[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Yes, but pace yourself, and ask the older pupils to demonstrate now and then. Strengthening the muscles around the joints is what helps most over time. I won't start any tablets today.",
      "start_timestamp": "07:00",
      "end_timestamp": "07:17",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Yes, I'd like to see you in four weeks, once we have the results.",
      "start_timestamp": "07:26",
      "end_timestamp": "07:34",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[3]",
        "follow_up[0]"
      ]
    }
  ],
